To decompose the mission description into a goal model for a multi-robot system, we need to identify the main objectives and break them down into sub-goals and tasks. Here's how the decomposition can be structured:

### Goals

| Goal ID | Goal Title                  | Text                                                                 | Runtime Annotation | Goal Type | Relation |
| ------- | --------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------ | --------- | -------- |
| G1      | Deliver Food                | Ensure food is delivered to the inpatient room.                      | -                  | Perform   | -        |
| G2      | Determine Retrieval Method  | Decide how the food will be retrieved (robot or human).              | FALLBACK(G2.1, G2.2) | Query     | G1       |
| G3      | Deliver Food to Table       | Deliver food directly to the room table using robot manipulation.    | -                  | Perform   | G2.1     |
| G4      | Coordinate Tray Retrieval   | Coordinate with humans or robots for tray retrieval if needed.       | FALLBACK(G4.1, G4.2) | Perform   | G2.2     |
| G5      | Track Meal Retrieval        | Track which meal is retrieved and alert if incorrect.                | -                  | Achieve   | G1       |
| G6      | Retrieve Dirty Dishes       | Retrieve dirty dishes from the room.                                 | -                  | Perform   | G1       |
| G7      | Determine Dish Retrieval Method | Decide how the dishes will be retrieved (unassisted, with robots, or with humans). | FALLBACK(G7.1, G7.2) | Query     | G6       |
| G8      | Unassisted Dish Retrieval   | Retrieve dishes unassisted.                                          | -                  | Perform   | G7.1     |
| G9      | Coordinate Dish Retrieval   | Coordinate with humans or robots for dish retrieval if needed.       | FALLBACK(G9.1, G9.2) | Perform   | G7.2     |

### Tasks

| Task ID | Task Title                  | Text                                                                 | Relation | Location          | Number of Robots |
| ------- | --------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------- | -------- | ----------------- | ---------------- |
| AT1     | Navigate to Inpatient Room  | Move to the designated inpatient room for delivery.                 | AND      | Hospital Room     | [1, n]           |
| AT2     | Manipulate Food Delivery    | Use robot skills to place food on the table.                        | AND      | Hospital Room     | 1                |
| AT3     | Communicate Retrieval Info  | Inform inpatient or staff about meal retrieval process.             | AND      | Hospital Room     | 1                |
| AT4     | Track Meal Retrieval        | Monitor which meal is retrieved and alert if incorrect.             | AND      | Hospital Room     | 1                |
| AT5     | Retrieve Dishes Unassisted  | Collect dirty dishes without assistance.                            | AND      | Hospital Room     | 1                |
| AT6     | Coordinate with Human       | Collaborate with a human to retrieve dishes.                        | AND      | Hospital Room     | [1, n]           |
| AT7     | Coordinate with Robot       | Collaborate with another robot to retrieve dishes.                  | AND      | Hospital Room     | [2, n]           |

### Logical Relationships

- **G1 -> G2, G5, G6 [AND]**
- **G2 -> G3, G4 [OR]**
- **G3 -> AT1, AT2 [AND]**
- **G4 -> G4.1, G4.2 [OR]**
  - **G4.1 -> AT3 [AND]**
  - **G4.2 -> AT6, AT7 [OR]**
- **G5 -> AT4 [AND]**
- **G6 -> G7 [AND]**
- **G7 -> G8, G9 [OR]**
- **G8 -> AT5 [AND]**
- **G9 -> G9.1, G9.2 [OR]**
  - **G9.1 -> AT6 [AND]**
  - **G9.2 -> AT7 [AND]**

This model ensures that all aspects of the mission are covered, with clear goals and tasks, and logical relationships between them.
